{
  "program": "COCRDLIC",
  "caseId": "case20",
  "description": "9500-FILTER-RECORDS at :1382-1407, reached with FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID. An eleven-digit numeric filter takes 2210-EDIT-ACCOUNT's success path at :1027-1028, so the browse still starts at the top of the file and every record read is compared: :1385-1391 excludes any record whose CARD-ACCT-ID differs, and an excluded record does not advance WS-SCRN-COUNTER because :1162 guards the placement. The filter is therefore applied in the program rather than by switching to the CARDAIX alternate-index path, and the whole file is still read - which is why the browse ends on ENDFILE and :1238-1240 moves 'NO MORE RECORDS TO SHOW' even though far fewer than seven rows were placed. 1300-SETUP-SCREEN-ATTRS takes WHEN FLG-ACCTFILTER-ISVALID at :845 and echoes the accepted filter back with DFHBMFSE rather than DFHRED, so no colour reaches ACCTSIDC at all. And :1027 moves the accepted filter into CDEMO-ACCT-ID, so the communication area carries the eleven digits forward - the rejection paths at :1011 and :1024 zero it instead, which is what separates a filter that was accepted from one that was not.",
